THIS FILE IS NOT COVERED BY THE REPOSITORY'S APACHE-2.0 LICENCE.

It is a screenplay — an original creative work, protected by copyright
from the moment it was written, and included here only because a format
for describing films needs at least one real film-length script to be
tested against. A feature screenplay is not source code and is not
licensed as if it were.

WHAT YOU MAY DO
---------------

You may copy, store and redistribute this file verbatim as part of this
repository or any fork of it, and you may use it to develop, test or
demonstrate software that reads, writes or converts SCF, Fountain or
related formats. That includes commercial software.

This grant exists so that forking the repository is lawful. An open
format that cannot be forked without infringing something is not open in
any way that matters, and a test corpus nobody may redistribute is a
test corpus nobody can run.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
-------------------

All other rights are reserved. In particular this grant does NOT permit
you to produce, perform, adapt, translate or publish the screenplay or
any part of it, to create derivative creative works from it, or to
distribute it as a standalone work outside this repository or a fork.

Nothing here grants any right to train a machine-learning model on this
file. That is neither permitted nor, by this document, conceded to be
something that would otherwise require permission.

NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTERS
---------------------

Conformance never depends on this file. The normative fixture is
`fixtures/hollow_creek.scf`, which is Apache-2.0 with the rest of the
repository, and the sixteen canonical query results are computed from
it. This screenplay is a regression baseline for the parser — 127 scene
headings, 45 locations, 27 speaking characters — and nothing in
`spec/conformance.md` refers to it.

The other files under `corpus/public/spec/` are hand-written test
fixtures rather than creative work, and are Apache-2.0.
